Not changed, but needs attention: the `MESSAGE_CODES` mapping at the bottom depends on Pydantic v1 error message text ("field required", "value is not a valid integer", "ensure this value has at least"). Pydantic v2 messages are different ("Field required", "Input should be a valid integer, ...", "String should have at least 3 characters"). Because the matching is case-sensitive prefix matching, under v2 every error will fall through to "INVALID" and the MISSING / NOT_AN_INTEGER / TOO_SHORT codes will silently stop being produced. This is a behavior change, not a deprecated API, and it is outside the listed finding, so I did not edit it. It should be fixed by matching on `err["type"]` (e.g. "missing", "int_parsing", "string_too_short") in a follow-up change, and tests should cover the error codes.

`Field(..., min_length=3)` is valid in v2 and was left as is. The model's `CreateUser` is a BaseModel subclass, so the finding is a true positive and not a false positive."}
